 dict(id="GE07", title="Office plate: Blender room, lights, two layers", needs=["GE03", "GE05", "GE06"],
  files=["tools/art/room_office.py", "tests/run_room_office.sh", "assets/art/rooms/office.png", "assets/art/rooms/office_front.png"],
  goal="Render the office hub tableau (see docs/art/GE.md 'Office') as two pixel-art layers: `office.png` (the whole room, window opening transparent so the game can draw a moving sky behind it, TV screen near-black) and `office_front.png` (only the two swivel chairs, drawn OVER the characters who sit in them seen from behind).",
  read=[BL, GE, "docs/art/ge_proto/room_office.py (the assembly script: layout rects, props and the four lights are all in it)", "tools/art/pixelbg.py and tools/art/check_room.py (GE03)", ROOMCLI],
  steps=[
   "Create `tools/art/room_office.py` from the prototype: imports `roomlib`, `roomkit_shell`, `roomkit_furn`, `roomkit_props`; arguments `--out <png> [--samples N] [--front]`; same layout constants WINDOW, POSTER, BOARD, TV_HOUSING, TV_SCREEN, TV_CAB, CABINET, GARAGE, KETTLE_TABLE, DESK, LAMP_X; the same props, bunting, four lights (sun through the blinds #ffe2b8 energy 2.6, warm desk lamp point light #ffab55 energy 360, cool TV area light #78b4ff energy 260, soft fill #ffe6c8 energy 500) and the layer logic (`--front` renders only objects whose name starts with `c_`; the default pass hides them). The prototype's final `PROJ` prints for the named objects can stay. `setup_render(..., transparent=True)`. Print `RENDERED <out>`.",
   "`tests/run_room_office.sh` (sh, repo root, `mkdir -p assets/art/rooms /tmp/ge07`): back pass `... room_office.py -- --out /tmp/ge07/office_raw.png --samples 64`, then `... pixelbg.py -- --in /tmp/ge07/office_raw.png --out assets/art/rooms/office.png --width 640 --colors 96 --dither 0.22`; front pass with `--front`, then pixelbg with `--colors 32 --out assets/art/rooms/office_front.png`.",
   "Then check the back plate: `check_room.py -- assets/art/rooms/office.png --size 640x360 --max-colors 96 --hole 40,275,60,38 --solid 600,100,100,40 --dark 482,196,286,210,16 --warm 330,300,120,60,30 --calm 0,0,1280,90,12 --bright 300,500,300,100,60` and require `ROOM OK`. (If a number fails, tune the matching light energy or colour in room_office.py by at most 30 percent and render again; do not edit the thresholds.) Check the front plate: `--size 640x360 --max-colors 32 --hole 0,0,1280,300 --solid 530,410,50,40` must be `ROOM OK`. Print `ROOM OFFICE OK`.",
   "Both PNGs are committed (about 100 to 250 KB each). Say in your summary: the `colors=` and `lum=` numbers that check_room printed. The planner looks at the pictures afterwards."],
  accept=["`sh tests/run_room_office.sh` prints `ROOM OFFICE OK`.", "`file assets/art/rooms/office.png assets/art/rooms/office_front.png` shows two PNGs of `640 x 360`."]),

